id: pm-rust-crash-lock-restart
title: Recover incomplete native lock initialization after process death
description: "The first native lock fsync follows a complete owner payload but leaves a fresh empty publication gate on process death. That gate blocks existing confirmed-dead-owner recovery and causes update/comment restart exit 4 while acknowledged item/history bytes remain intact. Recover only under the kernel lease with verified same-host original-process death and identity-checked empty-gate reclamation. Preserve unknown/live-owner refusals, immutable histories, exact restart references and the 50-writer no-loss contract; builds on #104."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[4]: crash-consistency,follow-up,"gh:unbraind/pm-rust#105",locks
created_at: "2026-10-21T22:16:11.158Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-24T23:14:03.134Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-24T21:48:10.461Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-23T21:02:58.000Z"
author: codex-agent
resolution: "Verified dead-owner restart reclaims only identity-checked incomplete native lock initialization under kernel ownership, preserving live/unknown-owner refusals and 50-writer no-loss histories."
expected_result: "The first native lock fsync follows a complete owner payload but leaves a fresh empty publication gate on process death. That gate blocks existing confirmed-dead-owner recovery and causes update/comment restart exit 4 while acknowledged item/history bytes remain intact. Recover only under the kernel lease with verified same-host original-process death and identity-checked empty-gate reclamation. Preserve unknown/live-owner refusals, immutable histories, exact restart references and the 50-writer no-loss contract; builds on #104."
actual_result: "https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/pull/105, merged 2026-10-23T21:02:58Z, merge 49b43605374e8cc103358221f9db9e9b434b1dbd: Verified dead-owner restart reclaims only identity-checked incomplete native lock initialization under kernel ownership, preserving live/unknown-owner refusals and 50-writer no-loss histories."
comments[16]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T22:19:53.971Z",codex-agent,"Overlap check: lock and initialization searches found no open item covering safe recovery from incomplete lock publication. This is distinct from text ownership refusal parity and completed owner-death locking work. The two measured failures are native update/comment at fsync ordinal 1, restart exit 4; all acknowledged item/history bytes remain intact. Repair policy is deliberately separate from the crash evidence harness."
  "2026-10-21T23:04:13.757Z",codex-agent,"Read both retained same-family update/comment fsync ordinal 1 cases and #104. The first fsync follows a complete owner-payload write; the fresh empty publication gate prevents the existing confirmed-dead-owner recovery. Plan: while holding the existing kernel lease, admit identity-checked empty-gate reclamation only for a confirmed dead same-host owner; retain TTL and unknown/live/nonempty-gate refusals. Add permanent independent replay cases, require every measured boundary to recover, and verify 50 simultaneous writers without Git. Targeted checks locally; unchanged-threshold release-check matrix remains the full CI gate. This branch builds on #104 and must merge after it."
  "2026-10-21T23:19:03.467Z",codex-agent,"The corrected synthetic corpus passes 20/20 injected kills with 20/20 acknowledged writes, history prefixes, exact reference states and restart receipts; both cross-runtime baseline byte and acknowledgement comparisons pass. The separate permanent update/comment first-fsync replay tests pass 2/2; the fresh-gate owner and lease guard unit test passes. The initial minimal fixture failed oracle settings validation and was corrected before proof. A default-budget standalone run timed out under local load; the supported 60000 ms process budget completed the corpus. No recovery invariant or coverage threshold was relaxed. Targeted Rust acceptance and behavioral revert proof are next."
  "2026-10-21T23:27:21.449Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof complete: replaced only mutation::acquire_lock_attempt with the #104 implementation, rebuilt using CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=2 cargo +1.90.0 build --locked --bin pm-rust, and ran node --test --test-name-pattern='retained (update|comment)' scripts/crash-harness.test.mts. Reverted: 0 passed, 2 failed, both actual restart exits 4. Restored and rebuilt: 2 passed, 0 failed. Tests and fixtures were unchanged. Full harness via the pinned PM linked runner passes 16/16 with zero skips; gate-focused unit selection passes 6/6; 50 writers preserve all 150 comments and the exact history chain. Shared-path ownership JSON refusal comparison passes exactly. The separate pre-existing comment diagnostic mismatch is retained on pm-rust-comment-lock-receipt; native legacy formatting is unchanged here. No PM CLI/SDK defect was identified."
  "2026-10-21T23:28:46.932Z",codex-agent,"Final pinned PM linked Rust acceptance passes: cargo +1.90.0 test --locked --test concurrency_contract --test parity_1021_contract with CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=2 and PM_RUST_REQUIRE_PUBLISHED_CLI=1 runs 2/2 concurrency tests plus 14/14 October 21 contract tests, zero failed or ignored. All 50 simultaneous writers retain 150/150 comments and history links without Git. Full harness 16/16, gate-focused unit selection 6/6 and restored independent replay tests 2/2 pass. Strict targeted Clippy, formatting, TypeScript checking, ESLint, changelog generation/check and immutable tracker-history prefix checks pass. Full unchanged-threshold release-check is delegated to the Linux/macOS/Windows CI matrix as requested; no merge or release."
  "2026-10-21T23:29:45.182Z",codex-agent,Local check-only health reports inherited history-chain warnings for pm-rust-bj7a and pm-rust-unih. An independent plain-directory archive of the unchanged #104 head reports the same warnings. Guidance/provenance/stale-item advisories and shared configuration drift also remain. No existing history was repaired or rewritten; the original restart-item stream remains an exact prefix of the appended history. CI's existing clone-local health setup remains authoritative for its gate. This is separate from the passing recovery and concurrency evidence.
  "2026-10-21T23:35:14.434Z",codex-agent,"Implementation and local verification are complete in PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/pull/105, based on main and explicitly dependent on #104 merging first. The final verification receipt will be kept in that PR with the exact-head CI run URL, per-platform test totals and all four coverage counts, linked from docs/CRASH_HARNESS.md. The Linux/macOS/Windows release-check matrix is still pending; no pending, canceled, skipped or unavailable reviewer result is treated as approval. Releasing the implementation claim for orchestrator verification while retaining in_progress status. No merge or release."
  "2026-10-22T11:34:12.928Z",codex-agent,"PR 105 integration round: pulled the remote head, confirmed zero review threads and no substantive CodeRabbit review body, then merged current origin/main a600bd8 and the completed PR 104 branch at 328ff009483d754b3e25412580495378025d5d87. Both merges were clean; main contributes its audited tracker reconciliation and the harness contributes the three typed-refusal fixes with four regressions. No recovery code or thresholds were changed in this round. Preserved the strict every-boundary recovery assertions and both permanent first-fsync replays. Running current-binary build, strict TypeScript/lint and the pinned-PM linked full crash harness, then the unchanged full release gate in CI given the demonstrated local cold-build contention. Existing original recovery revert receipts remain immutable."
  "2026-10-22T11:42:02.323Z",codex-agent,"Merged-head local acceptance passes: current native binary build; strict erasable TypeScript, ESLint, Rust fmt, diff check and isolated pinned-PM health. The existing linked full crash-harness command passed 20/20, zero failed or skipped, in about 215 seconds within its unchanged stored 300-second budget. This includes every measured crash boundary, exact acknowledged bytes/history/receipts, both permanent first-fsync replays and all four merged refusal regressions. No recovery function, original history, fixture, dependency pin or threshold was changed by this integration round, so no new behavioral-revert control is required; the original recovery proof and PR 104 guard proofs remain linked. Pushing the integrated candidate for unchanged just release-check in CI; the full gate is not yet claimed as passed."
  "2026-10-22T12:12:14.934Z",codex-agent,"Integrated code head 46178e2dae6468d1f71e18a23c9e608e19a48a56 passed the full Linux just release-check gate (https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/actions/runs/39772686608/job/119803873398). Ordinary and instrumented Rust runs each passed 580 tests across 22 suites, zero failed or ignored. Rust lines 14030/14030, functions 1467/1467, regions 23449/23449 and branches 3298/3298 are all 100 percent at unchanged thresholds. Strict TypeScript, ESLint and the merged Linux crash harness passed 20/20, zero failed or skipped, inside that gate. Audit, changelog and strict tracker health passed; the existing allowed RUSTSEC-2024-0449 advisory remains. macOS full gate also passed. This round has no review findings and no new recovery-code edits; original two-failure/two-restored recovery proof and merged PR 104 guard proofs remain intact. Releasing the claim and retaining in_progress; final receipt-head CI will be linked from PR 105. No replies/resolutions, PR merge or release."
  "2026-10-22T17:21:57.057Z",codex-agent,"Original stacked-PR instruction, follow-up to the completed PR 104 review round: pulled PR 105 remote head 53e4988, confirmed zero review threads and no substantive CodeRabbit review, verified main is already an ancestor, then merged PR 104 final head f555a4238fc4d0fa5768feaee0e81dce66031202 after all nine of its exact-head CI jobs passed. The merge is clean and brings the baseline_parity replay guide/docstring correction plus two documentation regressions and LF/CRLF checks. No Rust source changed in this integration. Existing recovery invariants, two permanent first-fsync replays and original independent recovery revert proof remain intact. Running current-binary build, strict TypeScript/lint and the unchanged 300-second linked full crash harness, followed by the full unchanged release gate."
  "2026-10-22T17:23:48.746Z",codex-agent,"Merged-head acceptance passes: current native build, strict erasable TypeScript, ESLint, required check-only tracker health, and the existing pinned-PM linked full crash suite. node --test scripts/crash-harness.test.mts passes 22/22 with zero failed/canceled/skipped in about 16 seconds inside its unchanged 300-second budget. Every measured crash boundary, both permanent update/comment first-fsync replays, exact bytes/history/receipts and the two merged guidance checks pass. All Rust source is byte-identical to 53e4988, so this integration adds no runtime fix or new runtime revert requirement; original recovery and inherited PR 104 documentation revert proofs remain valid and linked. Existing result-tracking policy is disabled; results are recorded here without changing it."
  "2026-10-22T17:23:49.343Z",codex-agent,"Releasing the integration claim with status retained in_progress for orchestrator verification. This branch now includes the completed PR 104 head f555a4238fc4d0fa5768feaee0e81dce66031202 and current main a600bd8. Fresh unchanged-threshold full just release-check CI will validate the pushed integration head; its exact receipts and counts will be recorded in PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/pull/105. Pending CI is not approval. No review reply/resolution, PR merge, release, dependency/threshold change or history rewrite."
  "2026-10-23T20:08:49.952Z",codex-agent,"PR 105 review round starts only after PR 110 completed its full exact-head CI gates and push. Pulled remote recovery head ca52b3608505542519781d6709799c163d9e01de. GraphQL returns zero review threads and no CodeRabbit review body; the latest CodeRabbit issue comment explicitly skips automatic review. The branch is four main commits behind and GitHub reports conflicts. Merge origin/main before code review, preserve both append-only tracker streams and the recovery/harness stack, regenerate the changelog inside the merge, then verify the complete PR diff, focused regressions and unchanged native release gate. Existing recovery and crash-boundary evidence remains historical until checked against the integrated candidate."
  "2026-10-23T20:17:51.120Z",codex-agent,"Merged main 300eaa9a9d06f0e2cfc6afcfa8b66492a960a77b with three conflicts resolved: retain both ignore lists and crash/benchmark recipes; retain the main non-git native process helper plus the branch requirement of 50 concurrent writers and three comments each. Expanded the expected marker set to all 150 entries so the merged test remains coherent and strict. Behavioral negative control restored only the old expected-set behavior in the concurrency test function: it compiled and failed with exit 101, actual 150 markers versus expected 50; restored the full set afterward. The integrated recovery negative control removed only the early confirmed-dead-owner gate admission from acquire_lock_attempt, rebuilt, and ran node --test --test-name-pattern=\"retained (update|comment)\" scripts/crash-harness.test.mts: two failures, both restart exit 4. Restored source/binary passed both cases (2/2). Whole-PR review retained lock identity/lease/refusal controls, exact receipt/history checks, typed harness refusals and no-git execution. Updated one stale harness comment to describe fixed reference invocations after main introduced shared journal recovery. All 78 branch and 80 main history streams remain exact byte prefixes; no history rewrite or repair. Strict TypeScript, ESLint, merge-time changelog check, and isolated required check-only health pass. Full linked acceptance and unchanged full CI gate follow."
  "2026-10-23T20:23:14.015Z",codex-agent,"Final integrated acceptance: all three pinned-PM linked commands passed, totaling 22 Linux crash-harness tests, 2 concurrency tests, 14 parity tests and 6 gate-focused unit tests (44 cases, zero failed or skipped). The concurrency assertion covers all 150 unique comments exactly once plus the complete 151-record history chain. Clippy retained its 100-line function limit: extracted the full expected marker set into documented expected_markers rather than relaxing lint. Repeating the helper-only stale-set behavioral control compiled and failed with exit 101, actual 150 versus expected 50; restored helper passed the linked 2+14 Rust acceptance again. Recovery proof remains two restart-exit-4 failures with only early dead-owner admission reverted, then two passes after restoring/rebuilding. Final strict all-target/all-feature Clippy, formatting, private rustdoc, strict erasable TypeScript, ESLint and isolated required tracker health pass. Merge-time changelog generation/check will be repeated after this final tracker write. Original JSON receipts and fixtures are untouched. The full unchanged just release-check matrix will run on the pushed integration head; no pending or skipped reviewer is counted as approval. Release the claim and retain in_progress for orchestrator verification."
